# Kingdom: Project Rules

## Stack
- Vite + TypeScript + Phaser 3, browser only, no backend
- Run: `npm run dev`. Deploys to GitHub Pages via .github/workflows/deploy.yml (`npx vite build`)
- PWA: public/manifest.webmanifest + public/sw.js (network-first offline cache). Icons are drawn in scripts/icons.mjs and emitted by a plugin in vite.config.ts (no image files in the repo)

## Structure (trust this, don't explore to confirm)
- src/main.ts: Phaser config, boots MapScene (CityScene sleeps until a city opens), registers the service worker (production only)
- src/world/: pure game logic, no Phaser imports
  - tile.ts: Tile type, terrain from height, yields, claim costs, walls, city levels (growth)
  - map.ts: WorldMap, generation, neighbors, hexDistance, raise/lower
  - units.ts: unit stats, jobs, move costs, reachable(), findPath() + routeTurns() for routes
  - game.ts: GameState: seats/players, turns, economy, claims, cities, training, combat, capture, growth, routes, win checks, DIFFICULTY
  - city.ts: City View rules: plots, terrain, neighbor/facing bonuses, auto-place
  - grid.ts: City Builder ground grid: size by highest level reached (7/9/11), plot and road tiles
  - ai.ts: rival AI, uses only public GameState methods
  - save.ts: localStorage save/load (key kingdom-save-v3), fills gaps from older saves
- src/scenes/: rendering and input only
  - MapScene.ts: hexes, borders, cities, units, overlays, routes, clicks, hover, camera, pinch zoom, hot-seat hand-off
  - CityScene.ts: the city screen (Phaser): ground grid, Keep, plots, roads, facing markers, people, pan + pinch zoom
  - CityView.ts: DOM header + side panel for the city screen (plot info, bonuses, build list), sleeps/wakes the map
  - citySprites.ts: pixel people inside cities
  - Hud.ts: DOM overlay (stats, bottom bar, selection panel sections, tooltip, idle prompt, pass screen, help)
  - Menu.ts: start menu (map size, players list, difficulty)
- src/game/ and other files in src/scenes/ are old unused stubs (break `npm run build`, safe to delete)

## Behavior rules
- Don't explore the project unless asked or a file is missing. Only touch files for the current request.
- One step at a time. No features I didn't ask for.
- World logic stays in src/world. Scenes read the world and call GameState methods.
- Never assume player 0 is "the human". Scenes act as `state.current` (MapScene `this.me`); check `players[p].isAI`.
- After changes, tell me what changed in 1-3 lines and how to test it.

## Game rules (current)
- Pointy-top odd-r hexes. Map sizes small 20x14, medium 30x20, large 44x30, huge 60x40
- Players: 1-4 seats, each a named Person or AI (options.seats). Seat 1 is always a person. 1 seat = sandbox. 2+ people = hot-seat: pass-the-device screen between people, log/win text uses names
- Difficulty (AI only) Easy (default) / Normal / Hard: AI income 0.7/1/1.25x, max troops 3/8/14, attacks from turn 45/22/14, AI land win off on Easy, builder jobs unlimited/3/3. Hard counters troops and retreats wounded units
- Gold: tile yields + city 3 + capital 5 + city level bonus. Food: capital 3, city 2, farm 3. Mines: 2 stone
- Land belongs to a city (tile.home). Claim land is a city action: unowned land within 3 hexes (4 at level 3+) touching that city's land, price +8% per tile bought
- Builder 15g: farm, mine, road, raise/lower, one job per turn, retires after its last job on Normal/Hard
- Settler: 10g + 10g per city, 3 turns, found 3+ hexes from other cities. Cities get random names (renameable)
- Walls are a city action: 5g + 10/20/30 stone, 3 levels, shield soaks damage first
- Troops: Swordsman 25g (beats Archer, captures), Archer 30g (range 2, beats Knight), Knight 45g (4 moves, beats Swordsman, captures)
- Cities regen 10/turn unless enemy troops within 2 hexes. A 0 HP city is captured by walking in. Capital capture eliminates the player
- Units heal 25% max HP per turn on their own land only
- City growth: spare food fills a growth bar (10/25/45/70), levels 1-5 Village..Metropolis: +gold, +food, +10 HP each, claim radius 4 at level 3, faster training at 5. Stalls under siege, capture drops a level
- Routes: select a unit, tap a far hex = preview (path, numbered turn stops), tap again = go. Moves itself at the start of each turn, re-planned every turn. Waits behind own units, routes around them after 2 waits, stops if enemies come within 2 hexes, ends next to enemy units/cities and never attacks by itself. X or any manual move/attack cancels
- Auto-select jumps to the next unit with work; Space checks idle units first (Hold skips them)
- Win: last kingdom standing, or hold 60% of the land. All people out = AI wins

## Roadmap
1-10 done (economy, builders, settlers, walls, troops, AI, difficulty, UI polish, city growth, routes), 11 hot-seat + PWA done
- In progress: City Builder (docs/CITY_BUILDER.md), ClickUp tasks 3-7, built on the dev branch
- Next ideas: per-player handicap (kids), troop ranks (XP per troop), new troops (Catapult, Boat, Medic), online play (Cloudflare Worker), terraforming tweaks
